In attempting to meet the wants and needs of the domestic population, on what basis do governments determine their program priorities to meet those needs:
- the impact of those priorities on the popularity of the government;
- the resources that are available;
- traditional priorities and practices; and,
- the efficiency of policies and their impact?

Are any of the following methods effective in restraining unjustified aggression by a nation:
- moral persuasion;
- economic boycotts;
- threat of international military action against the aggressor; or,
- international criticism?

